      },
      {
        "component": "O7 - pilot tuning of the 500 ms dwell (from 250/500/750 ms) and of the pinch-state thresholds (Sec. 3.2, 3.3.1)",
        "servable": false,
        "failed_criteria": [
          "screen_based",
          "no_experimenter",
          "apparatus_recovered"
        ],
        "why": "Dwell time could in principle be swept in a browser, but the thing being tuned is fingertip-distance thresholding on headset hand tracking. The paper reports only that the authors 'tested several variations' and selected an 'affordable distance', with no stated criterion or sample, so there is no procedure to serve even if the apparatus existed."
      },
